<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lesser Kabylia</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Little Kabylia</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lesser <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kabylia">Kabylia</a> is the eastern part of Kabylia in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algeria">Algeria</a>, a mountainous region around the Babor range between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bejaia">Béjaïa</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/setif">Sétif</a> and Jijel. Less isolated than <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greater-kabylia">Greater Kabylia</a> to the west, it was home from the 16th century to the Kingdom of Ait Abbas, whose lords later led the Mokrani revolt of 1871 against French rule.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lesser-kabylia.jpg" alt="Lesser Kabylia" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: PhR61 · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kabylie_B%C3%A9ja%C3%AFa.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
